1
00:00:18,902 --> 00:00:20,885
Enough!

2
00:00:22,139 --> 00:00:23,827
Why do you have this?

3
00:00:23,827 --> 00:00:25,032
What are you doing here?

4
00:00:25,033 --> 00:00:26,610
I didn't mean it.

5
00:00:26,610 --> 00:00:28,845
All of a sudden, there was a fire.

6
00:00:28,845 --> 00:00:31,515
Nero, calm down.

7
00:00:31,515 --> 00:00:33,250
Let's find out first what happened.

8
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:36,153
Maybe all of this was just an accident.

9
00:00:36,153 --> 00:00:39,323
This woman destroyed a place
that's very important to me.

10
00:00:39,323 --> 00:00:41,391
I'm sure Florence didn't mean to do this.

11
00:00:41,391 --> 00:00:43,994
We'll talk about this
when everyone has calmed down,

12
00:00:43,994 --> 00:00:47,631
so we'll know the root of this mess.

13
00:00:47,631 --> 00:00:51,969
Believe me, Grandpa,
even if I have calmed down,

14
00:00:51,969 --> 00:00:54,471
I don't want to see the face of this woman.

15
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:57,374
I have a bad feeling.

16
00:00:57,374 --> 00:01:00,277
Something wrong is happening.

17
00:01:00,277 --> 00:01:02,079
Go and call Florencia.

18
00:01:02,079 --> 00:01:06,750
The fact that she discovered your secret camp
is very impressive.

19
00:01:06,750 --> 00:01:10,854
It means, she's not only cooking for you.

20
00:01:10,854 --> 00:01:13,344
She's making an effort to get to know you.

21
00:01:13,344 --> 00:01:17,735
I'm sorry, Grandson,
I won't agree to kick Florence out.

22
00:01:17,735 --> 00:01:19,628
Because if we don't know how to forgive,

23
00:01:19,628 --> 00:01:23,000
we will not have a heart
deserving of happiness

24
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,601
and capable of love.

25
00:01:24,601 --> 00:01:26,770
Florence, have you given the rambutan?

26
00:01:26,770 --> 00:01:29,639
<i>Did the kids like it?</i>

27
00:01:29,639 --> 00:01:31,008
Yes, Mother, Father.

28
00:01:31,008 --> 00:01:34,745
He liked it very much
and consumed everything.

29
00:01:34,745 --> 00:01:36,313
He ate a lot.

30
00:01:36,313 --> 00:01:37,614
Florence, you're lying.

31
00:01:37,614 --> 00:01:39,149
Show yourself.

32
00:01:39,149 --> 00:01:40,817
I'll make a deal with you.

33
00:01:40,817 --> 00:01:42,619
Apologize to Nero first.

34
00:01:42,619 --> 00:01:46,857
Now, if he can't forgive you, then resign.

35
00:01:46,857 --> 00:01:50,460
I will even give you generous separation pay.

36
00:01:50,460 --> 00:01:52,696
But don't give up easily.

37
00:01:52,696 --> 00:01:54,297
Try it first.

38
00:01:54,297 --> 00:01:57,934
Give the person a chance to forgive.

39
00:01:57,934 --> 00:02:01,304
We all deserve a second chance.

40
00:02:01,304 --> 00:02:03,173
What are you doing here?

41
00:02:03,173 --> 00:02:05,242
Didn't I tell you
I don't want to see you anymore?

42
00:02:05,242 --> 00:02:07,978
One minute... that's all I ask from you.

43
00:02:07,978 --> 00:02:09,136
Just one minute.

44
00:02:09,136 --> 00:02:13,250
I just want to make up
for all the kindness you did for me.

45
00:02:13,250 --> 00:02:16,520
I hope when our paths cross again,

46
00:02:16,520 --> 00:02:19,166
you will no longer be mad at me.

47
00:02:19,167 --> 00:02:22,659
I heard Grandpa Garp is making
Florence apologize to Nero.

48
00:02:22,659 --> 00:02:24,194
Do you think Nero will forgive her?

49
00:02:24,194 --> 00:02:26,930
I don't think so, because knowing Nero,

50
00:02:26,930 --> 00:02:29,699
he's one of the toughest guys that I know.

51
00:02:29,699 --> 00:02:30,734
Let's make a bet.

52
00:02:30,734 --> 00:02:32,935
Let's see who will win.

53
00:03:27,124 --> 00:03:28,625
Hello?

54
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:30,293
<i>Hello, Don Rogelio. Sir.</i>

55
00:03:30,293 --> 00:03:31,795
<i>This is Mark.</i>

56
00:03:31,795 --> 00:03:35,065
<i>I've already run the aging program
that I told you about,</i>

57
00:03:35,065 --> 00:03:37,000
<i>the picture of Baby Celestina.</i>

58
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,370
<i>I've emailed you a picture
of how she will possibly look like</i>

59
00:03:40,370 --> 00:03:43,373
<i>in 17 years.</i>

60
00:03:43,373 --> 00:03:44,875
All right.

61
00:03:44,875 --> 00:03:46,842
Thank you.

62
00:04:24,086 --> 00:04:26,705
Alyanna, I need your help.

63
00:04:28,454 --> 00:04:31,490
If your daughter Celestina is still alive,

64
00:04:33,907 --> 00:04:35,515
you've got to help me.

65
00:04:36,972 --> 00:04:39,407
Point me in the right direction.

66
00:04:40,218 --> 00:04:45,368
Or better yet,
let our paths cross so I can save her.

67
00:04:47,307 --> 00:04:50,410
And give her the life
that you dreamed for her.

68
00:04:52,142 --> 00:04:55,311
Please, Alyanna...

69
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:59,782
Show me where your daughter is.

70
00:05:15,865 --> 00:05:17,934
Mother and Father,
I'm also excited to go out.

71
00:05:17,934 --> 00:05:19,122
I've been here for a long time.

72
00:05:19,122 --> 00:05:21,171
Well, Florence,
whatever you want to do, we'll do it.

73
00:05:21,171 --> 00:05:23,406
Whatever you want to eat, we'll eat it.

74
00:05:23,406 --> 00:05:26,800
Everything you want to buy,
we'll buy to make you happy.

75
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:33,315
Mother, Father, as long as I'm with you,
I'm already happy.

76
00:05:33,315 --> 00:05:34,351
Wow.

77
00:05:34,351 --> 00:05:36,136
- Come on.
- Let's go.

78
00:05:36,136 --> 00:05:39,055
Ouch, ouch...

79
00:05:48,748 --> 00:05:51,673
My favorite, fried chicken!

80
00:05:51,673 --> 00:05:54,771
Hey, Federico, that's not allowed.

81
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:57,907
Your heart will be fried, what's with you?

82
00:05:57,907 --> 00:06:00,709
Here, I brought something for you.

83
00:06:03,013 --> 00:06:04,281
That's delicious.

84
00:06:04,281 --> 00:06:05,892
Here's some more.

85
00:06:05,892 --> 00:06:07,883
Dessert.

86
00:06:10,931 --> 00:06:13,151
Mother, that's so sad.

87
00:06:13,151 --> 00:06:15,191
Vegetables for dessert?

88
00:06:15,191 --> 00:06:17,911
Okay, go ahead and tolerate each other.

89
00:06:17,911 --> 00:06:19,087
Not even just a little?

90
00:06:19,087 --> 00:06:20,466
- No.
- Just one bite, Mother?

91
00:06:20,467 --> 00:06:21,733
- Florence.
- It is not allowed.

92
00:06:21,734 --> 00:06:24,533
Don't worry, I'm doing okay.

93
00:06:24,534 --> 00:06:27,937
If there's something I can teach you
and you can apply it in your life,

94
00:06:27,937 --> 00:06:30,640
it is that all you need is a little imagination.

95
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:32,942
Imagination?

96
00:06:34,911 --> 00:06:37,513
The chicken is delicious.

97
00:06:38,281 --> 00:06:42,334
By the way, Mother, and Father,
here's my salary for you.

98
00:06:42,334 --> 00:06:43,680
Huh?

99
00:06:52,595 --> 00:06:54,831
Oh my!

100
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:57,500
Florence, this is a lot.

101
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,469
Did you save some for yourself?

102
00:06:59,469 --> 00:07:00,770
For your school?

103
00:07:00,770 --> 00:07:02,308
Mother, don't think about me,

104
00:07:02,308 --> 00:07:05,141
I don't have to spend so much on school.

105
00:07:05,141 --> 00:07:06,526
According to the dean,

106
00:07:06,526 --> 00:07:08,877
almost everything
is shouldered by the school.

107
00:07:08,877 --> 00:07:11,046
That's why I'm okay.

108
00:07:13,877 --> 00:07:16,947
Florence, thank you for your sacrifices.

109
00:07:16,947 --> 00:07:20,657
Father, I'm not the only one
making sacrifices for us.

110
00:07:20,657 --> 00:07:23,292
And like what you said just now,

111
00:07:23,292 --> 00:07:25,895
what we need in life is a little imagination.

112
00:07:25,895 --> 00:07:30,344
That's why every day I imagine
that I've graduated already,

113
00:07:30,344 --> 00:07:34,236
and that I've fulfilled
all our dreams in life.

114
00:07:35,588 --> 00:07:38,560
Florence, is there anything else you need?

115
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:41,211
Uniforms? Don't you need uniforms?

116
00:07:41,211 --> 00:07:43,077
Mother, Father, there's no uniform in GU.

117
00:07:43,077 --> 00:07:44,280
Initially, I thought I have to wear a uniform

118
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:47,016
because most of the schools have that, right?

119
00:07:47,016 --> 00:07:48,501
But the dean said to me,

120
00:07:48,501 --> 00:07:52,868
they don't want to destroy
the right of the student

121
00:07:52,868 --> 00:07:56,092
to their own individuality
and their freedom of expression.

122
00:07:56,092 --> 00:07:58,795
That's why, they don't insist on
wearing a uniform in the school.

123
00:07:58,795 --> 00:08:02,482
You should be who you are
when you go to school

124
00:08:02,482 --> 00:08:06,756
and this can help students gain confidence

125
00:08:06,756 --> 00:08:10,306
and they can build their self-image.

126
00:08:10,306 --> 00:08:12,742
- GU is really good.
- They're the best.

127
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:17,180
Florence, have you imagined
what you'd look like in school?

128
00:08:17,180 --> 00:08:19,449
Not yet. I'm still thinking about it.

129
00:08:19,449 --> 00:08:21,651
Well, I'll help you with that.

130
00:08:21,651 --> 00:08:23,553
I know a perfect spot.

131
00:08:23,553 --> 00:08:25,822
- We'll go shopping.
- Shopping!

132
00:08:25,822 --> 00:08:28,524
Let's eat first.

133
00:08:29,559 --> 00:08:30,968
What's that?

134
00:08:30,968 --> 00:08:33,730
Hey, Federico, I told you that's not allowed.

135
00:08:33,730 --> 00:08:35,334
Here, have this.

136
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:39,135
- Yummy.
- It's delicious.

137
00:08:39,135 --> 00:08:40,603
- I want that.
- One more.

138
00:08:40,603 --> 00:08:42,038
I want that.

139
00:08:42,038 --> 00:08:44,674
Hey, hey...
I already told you that's not allowed.

140
00:08:44,674 --> 00:08:46,508
Just eat this.

141
00:08:47,577 --> 00:08:50,146
My child... My child.

142
00:08:50,146 --> 00:08:52,615
Tada!

143
00:08:52,615 --> 00:08:55,985
This is the best place
to find your self-image

144
00:08:55,985 --> 00:08:58,321
- and individuality.
- Hello.

145
00:08:58,321 --> 00:08:59,889
What are you looking for?

146
00:08:59,889 --> 00:09:01,357
So are you ready, Florence?

147
00:09:01,357 --> 00:09:05,327
Yes, Mother. I'm ready to shop till we drop.

148
00:09:06,162 --> 00:09:07,497
So, what now?

149
00:09:07,497 --> 00:09:08,832
Let's go!

150
00:09:08,832 --> 00:09:11,567
- Let's go.
- Let's go. Where will we start?

151
00:09:12,373 --> 00:09:13,429
Let's start here.

152
00:09:13,429 --> 00:09:15,471
Let's go there.

153
00:09:18,498 --> 00:09:19,943
Which of the two do you like, Florence?

154
00:09:19,943 --> 00:09:22,812
This one, Mother. There.

155
00:09:22,812 --> 00:09:24,147
- Look, Florence.
- This one suits you.

156
00:09:24,147 --> 00:09:26,216
This is so much like you.

157
00:09:26,216 --> 00:09:27,750
Prof, pick me.

158
00:09:27,750 --> 00:09:29,919
I know the answer.

159
00:09:29,919 --> 00:09:31,788
- Pick me.
- Pick me.

160
00:09:31,788 --> 00:09:33,223
- Me!
- See, this is okay, right?

161
00:09:33,223 --> 00:09:35,525
Father, you look like Mother
with that outfit.

162
00:09:35,525 --> 00:09:36,993
Yes, that's possible.

163
00:09:36,993 --> 00:09:38,862
You look just like me.

164
00:09:38,862 --> 00:09:40,196
This is beautiful.

165
00:09:40,196 --> 00:09:41,975
It looks perfect on you.

166
00:09:41,975 --> 00:09:43,799
There you go.

167
00:09:45,235 --> 00:09:48,137
Father, let me borrow this.
Let's put this on mother.

168
00:09:48,137 --> 00:09:49,881
Wow.

169
00:09:49,881 --> 00:09:53,042
My child, why don't you introduce to me
the girl you're with?

170
00:09:53,042 --> 00:09:55,445
- The girl is beautiful, Father.
- Hey, you're something else.

171
00:09:55,445 --> 00:09:59,015
Your daughter is here. Later.

172
00:09:59,015 --> 00:10:00,433
Here, Florence...

173
00:10:00,433 --> 00:10:01,792
- It's beautiful.
- Mother.

174
00:10:01,792 --> 00:10:03,052
Isn't it too short?

175
00:10:03,052 --> 00:10:06,322
- No, if this fits me...
- But, Mother, my tummy will show.

176
00:10:06,322 --> 00:10:09,025
No. This is beautiful, Florence.

177
00:10:09,025 --> 00:10:10,159
- I'll just pair it
- This suits you really well.

178
00:10:10,159 --> 00:10:11,828
- with a high-waist skirt.
- Yes, that's perfect.

179
00:10:11,828 --> 00:10:14,097
- And then I'll wear a cardigan on it.
- And this too, it's beautiful also.

180
00:10:14,097 --> 00:10:15,164
This is better, Mother.

181
00:10:15,164 --> 00:10:17,467
- The other one is too short.
- It's good.

182
00:10:17,467 --> 00:10:18,835
Believe me, Florence...

183
00:10:18,835 --> 00:10:19,936
- Hey, this is okay.
- This is okay.

184
00:10:19,936 --> 00:10:21,004
Father!

185
00:10:21,004 --> 00:10:23,713
- This looks good...
- Father?

186
00:10:23,713 --> 00:10:25,241
- What?
- Federico!

187
00:10:25,241 --> 00:10:27,776
- What?
- What are you wearing?

188
00:10:28,645 --> 00:10:31,014
I just tried it on because it suits you.

189
00:10:31,014 --> 00:10:31,981
Everything, right?

190
00:10:31,981 --> 00:10:33,983
- That outfit is for me, Father?
- Yes.

191
00:10:33,983 --> 00:10:35,818
Father, since when did I wear hoops?

192
00:10:35,818 --> 00:10:37,053
Why? It's okay?

193
00:10:37,053 --> 00:10:38,821
- What's up?
- Hey, Federico!

194
00:10:38,821 --> 00:10:40,557
Did you pay for that already?

195
00:10:40,557 --> 00:10:42,025
- Oh my!
- I forgot.

196
00:10:42,025 --> 00:10:43,493
- Hurry. Pay for it.
- Hurry, Father.

197
00:10:43,493 --> 00:10:44,627
They might ask us for payment.

198
00:10:44,627 --> 00:10:47,650
Your father is something else.

199
00:11:07,056 --> 00:11:08,017
Why are you arrogant?

200
00:11:08,017 --> 00:11:09,352
So now I'm arrogant?

201
00:11:09,352 --> 00:11:10,753
- Do you have a problem with me?
- Do you have a problem with me?

202
00:11:10,753 --> 00:11:12,755
- You're been acting rude for a while now.
- That's you.

203
00:11:12,755 --> 00:11:13,790
Do you want us to fight here?

204
00:11:13,790 --> 00:11:14,791
- And now it's me?
- Do you want?

205
00:11:14,791 --> 00:11:15,992
Okay, let's finish this now.

206
00:11:15,992 --> 00:11:17,226
- What?
- James...

207
00:11:17,226 --> 00:11:19,262
- James, what's going on?
- You're so arrogant.

208
00:11:19,262 --> 00:11:21,264
He's so boastful.

209
00:11:21,264 --> 00:11:23,791
- Look. He's so arrogant.
- And I'm the boastful one?

210
00:11:23,791 --> 00:11:25,935
What's happening here?

211
00:11:25,935 --> 00:11:27,604
Nothing, Don Rogelio.

212
00:11:27,604 --> 00:11:29,405
This guy is so arrogant.

213
00:11:33,276 --> 00:11:35,311
Garpidio.

214
00:11:35,311 --> 00:11:36,877
Rogelio.

215
00:11:38,814 --> 00:11:40,245
Let's go, Baste.

216
00:11:40,245 --> 00:11:45,355
You will never win with people
who don't know how to admit their mistakes.

217
00:11:45,355 --> 00:11:47,423
James, let's go.

218
00:11:47,423 --> 00:11:51,461
You cannot win an argument with people
who cannot accept defeat.

219
00:11:51,461 --> 00:11:53,996
They'll just insist that they're right.

220
00:12:07,093 --> 00:12:08,611
We bought so much stuff.

221
00:12:08,611 --> 00:12:10,813
Where to next?

222
00:12:10,813 --> 00:12:11,848
- Let's try here?
- Over there.

223
00:12:11,848 --> 00:12:14,216
- That's a good place.
- Let's try this way.

224
00:12:15,618 --> 00:12:16,819
Where should we go?

225
00:12:16,819 --> 00:12:18,787
- Over there.
- There's a lot of good stuff there.

226
00:12:27,664 --> 00:12:29,032
Don Rogelio, where are you going?

227
00:12:29,032 --> 00:12:30,333
Excuse me.

228
00:12:30,333 --> 00:12:32,201
Excuse me...

229
00:12:33,089 --> 00:12:34,604
Yes, Sir?

230
00:12:34,604 --> 00:12:36,639
I'm sorry.

231
00:12:36,639 --> 00:12:39,007
I thought you were Celestina.

232
00:12:40,009 --> 00:12:41,706
Okay.

233
00:12:41,706 --> 00:12:44,313
Don Rogelio, do we have a problem?

234
00:12:44,313 --> 00:12:46,148
Are you looking for someone?

235
00:12:46,983 --> 00:12:47,984
No.

236
00:12:47,984 --> 00:12:49,885
Come on, let's go home.

237
00:13:05,768 --> 00:13:06,936
It's so cold.

238
00:13:06,936 --> 00:13:10,206
- Just leave your umbrellas there.
- Okay.

239
00:13:10,206 --> 00:13:12,508
Oh my God. We're all wet.

240
00:13:13,543 --> 00:13:15,378
It's embarrassing.

241
00:13:16,179 --> 00:13:18,347
Florence...

242
00:13:18,347 --> 00:13:20,816
thanks for all your help to us.

243
00:13:21,620 --> 00:13:24,652
Florence, next week, let's do this again.

244
00:13:24,652 --> 00:13:26,255
We miss you so much.

245
00:13:26,255 --> 00:13:28,858
Yes, Mother, me too. I miss you so much.

246
00:13:28,858 --> 00:13:31,828
And the way I miss you,
it's like kage bunshin technique.

247
00:13:31,828 --> 00:13:37,033
I miss you times two,
times two, times two, times two.

248
00:13:37,033 --> 00:13:40,870
Well, Florence, if you need anything,
just let us know.

249
00:13:40,870 --> 00:13:42,038
We'll be here right away.

250
00:13:42,038 --> 00:13:43,206
I know that.

251
00:13:43,206 --> 00:13:45,524
And I'm not afraid wherever I go.

252
00:13:45,524 --> 00:13:48,578
I can do anything

253
00:13:48,578 --> 00:13:51,881
because I know you and Father
are always there to back me up.

254
00:13:51,881 --> 00:13:53,416
Of course.

255
00:13:53,416 --> 00:13:54,869
Good thing you know.

256
00:13:54,869 --> 00:13:56,219
And because of that...

257
00:13:56,219 --> 00:13:59,744
- Goodbye hug.
- Goodbye hug.

258
00:13:59,744 --> 00:14:01,624
- Love you!
- Love you, Mother.

259
00:14:01,624 --> 00:14:04,927
- You take care of yourself here.
- Yes, Mother.

260
00:14:04,927 --> 00:14:06,329
- I love you, my child.
- I love you, Father.

261
00:14:06,329 --> 00:14:08,354
Always remember that.

262
00:14:09,752 --> 00:14:11,768
Take care and don't get wet.

263
00:14:11,768 --> 00:14:13,019
It's embarrassing.

264
00:14:13,019 --> 00:14:16,655
- Bye, my child.
- Bye, Mother. Take care.

265
00:14:19,336 --> 00:14:22,171
Take care, Mother and Father.

266
00:14:31,437 --> 00:14:33,939
Well, well, well.

267
00:14:35,725 --> 00:14:37,331
You're back.

268
00:14:37,331 --> 00:14:38,861
Yes, Ms. Serafica.

269
00:14:38,861 --> 00:14:42,297
I bought something for you.

270
00:14:42,965 --> 00:14:44,222
I remembered you.

271
00:14:44,222 --> 00:14:48,800
People wearing that are cool,
like Ms. Gretchen Barretto level.

272
00:14:48,800 --> 00:14:51,040
I'll make it up to you next time.

273
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:52,675
I couldn't find any.

274
00:14:52,675 --> 00:14:54,577
That's okay.

275
00:14:54,577 --> 00:14:56,646
Thank you.

276
00:14:56,646 --> 00:14:58,514
You're welcome.

277
00:14:58,514 --> 00:15:04,320
Florence, Dencio will bring
the boys to school tomorrow.

278
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:07,523
And James, the other driver
will drive you to school.

279
00:15:07,523 --> 00:15:09,559
Me? He'll bring me to school?

280
00:15:09,559 --> 00:15:11,694
- Yes.
- No need, Ma'am Serafica.

281
00:15:11,694 --> 00:15:16,065
I don't want the people in school
to think that I'm rich too.

282
00:15:16,065 --> 00:15:17,700
Are you sure?

283
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:19,435
Yes. Don't worry.

284
00:15:19,435 --> 00:15:20,942
I'll manage.

285
00:15:20,942 --> 00:15:24,373
Grandpa Garp has already
offered a lot of help.

286
00:15:24,373 --> 00:15:26,976
I can go to school on my own,

287
00:15:26,976 --> 00:15:30,613
so I won't disturb you and Mr. James.

288
00:15:30,613 --> 00:15:33,316
Okay, if that's your decision.

289
00:15:33,316 --> 00:15:35,718
- Ma'am Serafica?
- All right.

290
00:15:35,718 --> 00:15:38,221
I also want to thank you.

291
00:15:38,221 --> 00:15:42,415
I appreciate what you're doing
for me right now.

292
00:15:43,492 --> 00:15:45,995
Oh, by the way, Florence.

293
00:15:45,995 --> 00:15:47,266
What?

294
00:15:48,313 --> 00:15:49,966
Good luck.

295
00:15:49,966 --> 00:15:52,034
I'm rooting for you.

296
00:15:52,910 --> 00:15:55,700
I hope all your dreams will come true.

297
00:15:55,701 --> 00:15:57,666
Thank you.

298
00:15:57,667 --> 00:15:59,090
You can retire now.

299
00:15:59,091 --> 00:16:00,399
Goodnight.

300
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:01,743
- Goodnight.
- I'll make it up to you

301
00:16:01,743 --> 00:16:04,347
when there are new arrivals,
so that it'll be good.

302
00:16:04,347 --> 00:16:06,348
Goodnight.

303
00:16:23,766 --> 00:16:25,334
Good Morning, Florence.

304
00:16:25,334 --> 00:16:28,737
Are you ready to conquer the world?

305
00:16:33,375 --> 00:16:34,710
Mr. Dove.

306
00:16:34,710 --> 00:16:37,705
What's my letter for today?

307
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:39,815
Hey, you might hit your head.

308
00:16:39,815 --> 00:16:42,585
What's my letter for today?

309
00:16:42,585 --> 00:16:45,087
Thank you, Mr. Dove.

310
00:16:48,491 --> 00:16:51,293
Break a leg, see you at school.

311
00:16:53,954 --> 00:16:56,132
Break a leg.

312
00:16:56,132 --> 00:16:57,433
Are you ready, Florence?

313
00:16:57,433 --> 00:16:59,702
If you're ready give me an F.

314
00:16:59,702 --> 00:17:00,770
Give me an L.

315
00:17:00,770 --> 00:17:05,066
Give me an O, R, E, N, C, E!

316
00:17:05,067 --> 00:17:08,766
I'm Florence Dela Cruz
and I'm going to school.

317
00:17:08,767 --> 00:17:09,801
I'm best in math,

318
00:17:09,801 --> 00:17:13,867
and of all the good things I can do,
I can be your friend!

319
00:17:13,868 --> 00:17:16,852
Go, Florence! Go!

320
00:18:48,010 --> 00:18:50,612
So, guys, we're on our own for now.

321
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:56,934
Look at what we have here, Aira.

322
00:18:56,934 --> 00:19:01,157
Nero looks as hot as ever.

323
00:19:01,157 --> 00:19:06,228
If you compare it to tennis,
he is a Nadal, a Djokovic,

324
00:19:06,228 --> 00:19:07,630
and a Federer.

325
00:19:07,630 --> 00:19:10,399
He occupies all my top three.

326
00:19:10,399 --> 00:19:12,927
And my fourth and fifth.

327
00:19:12,927 --> 00:19:15,396
And look at Tristan.

328
00:19:15,396 --> 00:19:17,406
Has he been working out?

329
00:19:17,406 --> 00:19:22,211
Looks like there's a lot of stuff that grew
and became hard on him.

330
00:19:22,211 --> 00:19:24,447
Do you want to have lunch together?

331
00:19:24,447 --> 00:19:26,552
Aren't you tired of that?

332
00:19:26,552 --> 00:19:27,767
Exactly.

333
00:19:27,767 --> 00:19:30,326
We've been eating together the whole summer.

334
00:19:30,326 --> 00:19:32,888
Maybe this is a welcome respite
from all that...

335
00:19:32,888 --> 00:19:34,390
cheesiness.

336
00:19:34,390 --> 00:19:39,861
Not to mention... Aldus is still being Aldus.

337
00:19:40,740 --> 00:19:43,099
You're right about that.

338
00:19:43,099 --> 00:19:46,301
I'll take Aldus any time of the day.

339
00:19:47,138 --> 00:19:51,560
Not to mention, Owen.

340
00:19:52,975 --> 00:19:56,583
Exactly, there's nothing we can say.

341
00:19:56,583 --> 00:19:59,779
We're out of words.

342
00:19:59,779 --> 00:20:04,920
I disagree but yes,
it's like I don't want to see your faces.

343
00:20:04,920 --> 00:20:09,792
And look at Troy,
he seems like he is his usual fun self.

344
00:20:09,792 --> 00:20:11,494
I like some fun.

345
00:20:11,494 --> 00:20:14,396
Do you like some fun, Aira?

346
00:20:14,396 --> 00:20:17,165
I was born to be fun.

347
00:20:18,134 --> 00:20:19,748
How about you, Nero?

348
00:20:19,748 --> 00:20:22,071
I don't know any of you.

349
00:20:22,071 --> 00:20:23,939
So, let's go.

350
00:20:26,133 --> 00:20:31,067
[Gyronella University]

351
00:20:32,933 --> 00:20:34,934
Hot.

352
00:20:46,061 --> 00:20:50,265
What in the name of?

353
00:20:53,903 --> 00:20:55,937
What is that?

354
00:20:57,973 --> 00:21:00,175
Look at her.

355
00:21:06,803 --> 00:21:09,852
Mister, I'll get off here.

356
00:21:09,852 --> 00:21:11,020
Next time again.

357
00:21:11,020 --> 00:21:12,555
Here's my payment. Take care.

358
00:21:12,555 --> 00:21:14,311
Oh my God.

359
00:21:18,763 --> 00:21:21,664
Mother, Father, this is it!

360
00:21:21,664 --> 00:21:23,699
I'm here in GU.

361
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:26,335
I'll do my best for our future.

362
00:21:26,335 --> 00:21:29,104
This is the first day
for the rest of our lives.

363
00:21:29,104 --> 00:21:32,374
This is the start
of a new chapter of success!

364
00:21:32,374 --> 00:21:34,143
Please go to our booth.

365
00:21:34,143 --> 00:21:35,599
Booth?

366
00:21:37,644 --> 00:21:39,232
Okay.

367
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:46,622
Looks like our beloved university
has a new charity case.

368
00:21:46,622 --> 00:21:47,850
You can say that again.

369
00:21:47,850 --> 00:21:51,159
Should we put her on our blacklist?

370
00:21:52,494 --> 00:21:55,397
Looks like it'll be fun
to play a prank on her.

371
00:21:55,397 --> 00:21:57,264
Let's not waste our time.

372
00:21:57,264 --> 00:22:00,217
Besides, we still have one more target.

373
00:22:00,217 --> 00:22:03,420
And we need to focus our time on her.

374
00:22:04,255 --> 00:22:09,378
And from what I heard,
she's not following our orders.

375
00:22:09,378 --> 00:22:13,249
Looks like we need to teach her a lesson.

376
00:22:13,249 --> 00:22:14,817
I agree.

377
00:22:14,817 --> 00:22:16,751
Yeah, for sure.

378
00:22:27,429 --> 00:22:29,109
- I have a lot.
- Please go to our booth.

379
00:22:29,109 --> 00:22:30,432
Okay.

380
00:22:30,432 --> 00:22:32,700
I have a lot of places to go.

381
00:22:34,801 --> 00:22:37,934
[Gyronella University]

382
00:22:55,024 --> 00:22:59,227
<i>What do you think happened
for me to deserve this?</i>

383
00:23:08,771 --> 00:23:10,918
Miss, where is the Com Arts Building?

384
00:23:10,918 --> 00:23:12,541
Just follow the people.

385
00:23:12,541 --> 00:23:13,993
Wow, great.

386
00:23:13,993 --> 00:23:16,613
Just follow the people. All right.

387
00:23:19,148 --> 00:23:21,416
You think you're being smart?

388
00:23:22,051 --> 00:23:25,487
Stop acting like you belong here.

389
00:23:25,487 --> 00:23:27,356
No one likes you.

390
00:23:27,356 --> 00:23:30,125
If your parents didn't win the lottery,

391
00:23:30,125 --> 00:23:32,533
I doubt you can even afford to be here.

392
00:23:32,533 --> 00:23:33,924
Exactly.

393
00:23:34,797 --> 00:23:38,421
But it doesn't mean that
just because you can pay the tuition here,

394
00:23:38,421 --> 00:23:41,587
you can pretend like you're one of us.

395
00:23:41,587 --> 00:23:45,263
You will never be one of us.

396
00:23:45,263 --> 00:23:46,622
True.

397
00:23:46,622 --> 00:23:48,865
You can dress well.

398
00:23:48,865 --> 00:23:55,116
You can buy expensive stuff,
but inside you're still garbage.

399
00:23:55,951 --> 00:23:57,125
True.

400
00:23:57,125 --> 00:23:59,047
Exactly.

401
00:24:01,016 --> 00:24:03,124
What are you doing?

402
00:24:06,995 --> 00:24:10,165
Look who's here.

403
00:24:10,165 --> 00:24:13,268
The new attention-seeker.

404
00:24:16,405 --> 00:24:19,202
Shoo, girl, shoo!

405
00:24:19,202 --> 00:24:22,310
Mind your own business, please.

406
00:24:30,103 --> 00:24:33,505
Do you know my father's favorite saying?

407
00:24:35,624 --> 00:24:39,761
The way to the heart of a man or woman
is through their stomach.

408
00:24:40,529 --> 00:24:41,964
What?

409
00:24:42,931 --> 00:24:46,502
- She's kidding.
- What are you talking about?

410
00:24:46,502 --> 00:24:49,438
But I don't think that applies to you

411
00:24:49,438 --> 00:24:52,941
because it seems like your tummy
and intestines are not good.

412
00:24:52,941 --> 00:24:56,345
It looks like there's a blockage
going to your heart as well.

413
00:24:56,345 --> 00:24:59,047
So, what's more applicable to you is...

414
00:24:59,047 --> 00:25:01,483
"the only thing necessary
for the triumph of evil

415
00:25:01,483 --> 00:25:03,730
is for good men to do nothing."

416
00:25:03,730 --> 00:25:07,109
And with cases like this
that you're bullying someone

417
00:25:07,109 --> 00:25:09,024
and there's a witness like me

418
00:25:09,024 --> 00:25:12,293
when we won't do anything and be quiet...

419
00:25:14,801 --> 00:25:16,487
Oops!

420
00:25:18,967 --> 00:25:21,603
What? You'll take a video of me?

421
00:25:21,603 --> 00:25:23,124
No.

422
00:25:26,267 --> 00:25:28,467
[Dean]

423
00:25:34,049 --> 00:25:35,651
Dean!

424
00:25:35,651 --> 00:25:37,553
There are students here
who are bullying someone.

425
00:25:37,553 --> 00:25:40,456
I pity the girl,
she's on the verge of tears, Dean.

426
00:25:40,456 --> 00:25:43,558
- Let's go, girls!
- There are five of them.

427
00:25:46,414 --> 00:25:48,297
They think they're so brave.

428
00:25:48,297 --> 00:25:50,727
Hey, wait, where are you going?

429
00:25:50,727 --> 00:25:52,228
That's just a joke. Don't be scared.

430
00:25:52,228 --> 00:25:54,633
I didn't really call the dean.

431
00:25:54,634 --> 00:25:58,133
And if it's true that I called him,
there's no reason for you to be scared.

432
00:25:58,133 --> 00:26:01,910
You're the one being bullied.
They should be the one's who are worried.

433
00:26:01,910 --> 00:26:02,911
I'm Florence by the way.

434
00:26:02,911 --> 00:26:05,299
What are you doing?

435
00:26:05,300 --> 00:26:08,266
Do you have any idea what you just did?

436
00:26:08,267 --> 00:26:11,920
Yes, I saw them picking on you,
so I scared them,

437
00:26:11,920 --> 00:26:13,821
so they'll stop bullying you.

438
00:26:14,585 --> 00:26:16,091
Obviously, you're new here.

439
00:26:16,091 --> 00:26:18,633
You don't know who you're fighting with.

440
00:26:18,634 --> 00:26:22,366
Next time, just mind your own business, okay?

441
00:26:22,367 --> 00:26:27,333
Because of what you did,
you just made my situation worse.

442
00:26:27,334 --> 00:26:30,539
So be careful
because you'll also get in trouble

443
00:26:30,539 --> 00:26:33,541
and it seems that they'll pick on you next.

444
00:26:42,451 --> 00:26:46,654
<i>What do you think happened
for me to deserve this?</i>

445
00:26:49,591 --> 00:26:51,659
That's bad.

446
00:26:52,494 --> 00:26:55,263
How is the view from the floor?

447
00:27:00,469 --> 00:27:02,758
Why do you keep on changing your clothes?

448
00:27:02,758 --> 00:27:04,960
It's none of your business.

449
00:27:14,723 --> 00:27:16,387
Hey!

450
00:27:16,387 --> 00:27:18,854
What are you looking at?

451
00:27:18,854 --> 00:27:22,991
Owen, please, don't cramp my style.

452
00:27:22,991 --> 00:27:24,942
Why are you here?

453
00:27:24,942 --> 00:27:27,662
We've already talked
and we don't know each other.

454
00:27:34,536 --> 00:27:36,638
Her name is Sophia.

455
00:27:36,638 --> 00:27:38,332
Her family owns a coffee shop chain

456
00:27:38,332 --> 00:27:41,043
and I think they have a farm in Batangas.

457
00:27:41,043 --> 00:27:43,365
She's my classmate in Russian Literature.

458
00:27:43,365 --> 00:27:44,747
She owes me.

459
00:27:44,747 --> 00:27:48,154
I helped her deconstruct Dostoyevsky.

460
00:27:48,154 --> 00:27:50,055
Do you want me to introduce you?

461
00:27:50,055 --> 00:27:53,221
Or never mind,
since we don't know each other?

462
00:27:53,221 --> 00:27:55,857
What do you need?

463
00:27:55,857 --> 00:27:57,359
I'm just worried about Florence.

464
00:27:57,359 --> 00:27:59,411
Stop acting like her boyfriend.

465
00:27:59,411 --> 00:28:01,614
I'm not acting like her boyfriend.

466
00:28:01,614 --> 00:28:03,715
But have you seen what she looks like?

467
00:28:04,660 --> 00:28:07,486
Yeah, she was just being herself.

468
00:28:07,486 --> 00:28:10,422
Exactly, she's being herself,

469
00:28:10,422 --> 00:28:12,925
so she's painting herself as a target.

470
00:28:12,925 --> 00:28:15,313
It's like she's seeking attention
so the rich and obnoxious students

471
00:28:15,313 --> 00:28:17,329
can pick on her.

472
00:28:17,329 --> 00:28:20,499
How dare you suggest that I'm evil.

473
00:28:20,499 --> 00:28:22,568
What do you know?

474
00:28:22,568 --> 00:28:26,037
That I'm the villain in this story?

475
00:28:26,939 --> 00:28:28,274
I told you.

476
00:28:28,274 --> 00:28:34,647
The first time I saw her,
it looks like this one is bad news.

477
00:28:34,647 --> 00:28:37,159
You want attention, right?

478
00:28:37,159 --> 00:28:41,520
Now, we'll pay attention to you.

479
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:46,559
The good news is, I am here to warn you.

480
00:28:46,559 --> 00:28:51,130
The bad news is,
I'm also about to destroy you.

481
00:28:51,130 --> 00:28:57,001
Correction, we are about to destroy you.

482
00:28:57,937 --> 00:29:02,308
We will make sure that
your life here will be hell.

483
00:29:02,308 --> 00:29:05,882
And it will be so bad that
you don't have any choice

484
00:29:05,882 --> 00:29:07,947
but to transfer to a new school.

485
00:29:07,947 --> 00:29:09,641
Right.

486
00:29:09,641 --> 00:29:12,176
So, good luck.

487
00:29:15,321 --> 00:29:17,241
- Deserve.
- Deserve.

488
00:29:18,490 --> 00:29:20,358
- Deserve.
- Deserve.

489
00:29:22,194 --> 00:29:24,429
Let's go, girls.

490
00:29:29,038 --> 00:29:32,271
We should've asked her to come with us.

491
00:29:32,271 --> 00:29:35,666
So this whole university knows
she's one of us...

492
00:29:35,666 --> 00:29:38,119
and no one will try to bother her.

493
00:29:38,119 --> 00:29:40,446
You know that's one thing she hates the most.

494
00:29:40,446 --> 00:29:43,215
Have you forgotten how many times
she reminded you

495
00:29:43,215 --> 00:29:45,449
that when we get to the university,

496
00:29:45,449 --> 00:29:48,554
we don't know each other?

497
00:29:48,554 --> 00:29:50,897
Hey, you Ferell guys,

498
00:29:50,897 --> 00:29:53,270
when we get to the school,
we don't know each other.

499
00:29:53,270 --> 00:29:55,817
You don't know me, and I don't know you too.

500
00:29:55,817 --> 00:29:58,997
Why? Because the students there
might think that I'm as arrogant

501
00:29:58,997 --> 00:30:01,199
and hard-headed as all of you.

502
00:30:02,468 --> 00:30:05,204
That's why she refused
to hitch a ride with us,

503
00:30:05,204 --> 00:30:07,340
no matter how hard we tried to convince her.

504
00:30:07,340 --> 00:30:10,926
And do you really think that will help her?

505
00:30:10,926 --> 00:30:13,277
There are a lot of people
who are jealous of us, Ferells.

506
00:30:13,277 --> 00:30:17,184
And being associated with us
might not be so good for her.

507
00:30:17,184 --> 00:30:20,254
And for sure,
people will start asking questions.

508
00:30:20,254 --> 00:30:22,394
Like, who is she?

509
00:30:22,394 --> 00:30:24,527
Why is she connected with us?

510
00:30:24,527 --> 00:30:27,292
Why is Grandpa sending her to school?

511
00:30:27,292 --> 00:30:31,697
And I'm sure this can create
an issue for our family.

512
00:30:31,697 --> 00:30:35,337
And the last we need
is another rumor against our family.

513
00:30:36,244 --> 00:30:38,503
I still worry about Grandpa's heart.

514
00:30:40,405 --> 00:30:45,158
I know that,
but are we really letting Florence be?

515
00:30:45,158 --> 00:30:47,681
Rich people are the worse.

516
00:30:47,681 --> 00:30:50,416
Sooner or later, someone will target her.

517
00:30:50,416 --> 00:30:54,018
It's just a matter of time before someone
makes her life here a nightmare.

518
00:30:56,454 --> 00:30:57,922
It's like this, Bro.

519
00:30:57,922 --> 00:30:59,824
Look at it this way.

520
00:30:59,824 --> 00:31:03,828
Maybe the people here at the University
should worry about Florence.

521
00:31:03,828 --> 00:31:05,029
What do you mean?

522
00:31:05,029 --> 00:31:08,566
Do you think Florence is the kind of person

523
00:31:08,566 --> 00:31:12,203
who will just let others step on her?

524
00:31:12,203 --> 00:31:15,974
Do you think that Florence
is the type of person...

525
00:31:15,974 --> 00:31:18,876
who will not fight back
if someone is trying to oppress her?

526
00:31:19,811 --> 00:31:23,749
If there's one person who can fight back,
that's Florence.

527
00:31:23,749 --> 00:31:26,439
Because in the short period
that we've known her,

528
00:31:26,439 --> 00:31:28,720
she's the kind of person
who you can't destroy

529
00:31:28,720 --> 00:31:30,754
even if you hit her several times.

530
00:32:42,801 --> 00:32:44,563
Hey!

531
00:32:44,563 --> 00:32:46,532
You already saw that I fell,

532
00:32:46,532 --> 00:32:49,701
and now you're asking me
to hold on to your drink?

533
00:32:49,701 --> 00:32:53,370
You're really useless.
You want me to throw your garbage.

534
00:33:06,517 --> 00:33:11,288
Ah, so he's sweet...

535
00:33:12,256 --> 00:33:14,191
So that's why.

536
00:33:15,931 --> 00:33:18,206
You better hurry because
Don Ferell is about to eat.

537
00:33:18,206 --> 00:33:19,963
Don't forget the water, please.

538
00:33:19,963 --> 00:33:21,998
- Yes.
- Okay.

539
00:33:25,303 --> 00:33:27,839
Good morning, Don Ferell.

540
00:33:27,839 --> 00:33:30,942
- Good morning.
- Your breakfast is ready.

541
00:33:30,942 --> 00:33:33,444
Who cooked? You?

542
00:33:33,444 --> 00:33:36,748
No, Sir. It was still Florence.

543
00:33:36,748 --> 00:33:38,649
Huh? How?

544
00:33:38,649 --> 00:33:42,286
Well, she woke up early to prepare.

545
00:33:42,286 --> 00:33:45,757
As a matter of fact,
she already cooked your lunch.

546
00:33:45,757 --> 00:33:50,695
And she left me detailed instructions
on how to heat up your food.

547
00:33:50,695 --> 00:33:52,864
Very good girl.

548
00:33:52,864 --> 00:33:54,899
She's special.

549
00:33:56,125 --> 00:33:57,769
She deserves it.

550
00:33:57,769 --> 00:33:59,203
She totally deserves it.

551
00:33:59,203 --> 00:34:02,440
Yeah, I mean we were
minding our own business,

552
00:34:02,440 --> 00:34:05,276
and then she suddenly meddles.

553
00:34:05,276 --> 00:34:07,211
Exactly.

554
00:34:08,479 --> 00:34:10,907
She's not aware of her place here.

555
00:34:10,907 --> 00:34:14,152
She labeled us as if we were
the villains in her life.

556
00:34:14,152 --> 00:34:18,389
Well, if that's what she believes,
then I guess we should play the part.

557
00:34:18,389 --> 00:34:19,849
- I agree.
- Right?

558
00:34:19,849 --> 00:34:24,294
Embrace our roles
as the villains in the life of that squatter.

559
00:34:25,797 --> 00:34:27,056
Oh.

560
00:34:28,005 --> 00:34:31,435
Are you guys thinking of what I'm thinking?

561
00:34:32,303 --> 00:34:34,005
Yes.

562
00:34:34,005 --> 00:34:36,874
We are so sisters to the top of Everest

563
00:34:36,874 --> 00:34:38,709
because I can read what you want.

564
00:34:38,709 --> 00:34:40,545
Yeah.

565
00:34:40,545 --> 00:34:45,903
I think it's time to use our network.

566
00:34:45,903 --> 00:34:48,497
Aylip's network of horror.

567
00:34:49,320 --> 00:34:50,988
Game?

568
00:34:50,988 --> 00:34:54,224
Game. What are we waiting for?

569
00:34:58,367 --> 00:35:02,000
[TWPS]

570
00:35:07,762 --> 00:35:09,563
Nice.

571
00:35:10,262 --> 00:35:13,502
So, what do you think?

572
00:35:13,502 --> 00:35:15,105
That looks awesome, Ash.

573
00:35:15,105 --> 00:35:17,285
Very promising idea.

574
00:35:17,285 --> 00:35:20,605
It will be our University's official channel.

575
00:35:20,605 --> 00:35:26,167
I'll make content about our university,
everything GU.

576
00:35:26,167 --> 00:35:28,662
I'll review our food here in the cafeteria,

577
00:35:28,662 --> 00:35:31,932
news about school activities,
and places to hang out in GU.

578
00:35:31,932 --> 00:35:34,983
And of course, a profile piece...

579
00:35:34,983 --> 00:35:39,239
of the coolest students
here in the university, like us.

580
00:35:39,239 --> 00:35:42,041
Why are you telling me this?

581
00:35:42,983 --> 00:35:47,214
Well, the truth is, I need a partner.

582
00:35:47,214 --> 00:35:50,584
As much as I want to,
it's not just my face that will carry this.

583
00:35:50,584 --> 00:35:55,696
I need the gravitas of a Ferell

584
00:35:55,696 --> 00:35:58,859
so there's someone who will watch my content.

585
00:35:58,859 --> 00:35:59,926
No.

586
00:35:59,926 --> 00:36:01,628
No, straight away?

587
00:36:01,628 --> 00:36:02,996
Think about it.

588
00:36:02,996 --> 00:36:06,799
I go live tonight
and you can join me anytime.

589
00:36:06,799 --> 00:36:10,236
I'm sorry, Ash...
but that's not my cup of tea.

590
00:36:10,236 --> 00:36:12,804
The last thing I want to do
is face the camera.

591
00:36:15,074 --> 00:36:18,511
What about... what about him?

592
00:36:18,511 --> 00:36:20,446
That's even more difficult.

593
00:36:20,446 --> 00:36:22,114
I don't think that's possible.

594
00:36:22,114 --> 00:36:24,550
Why so?

595
00:36:24,550 --> 00:36:30,323
And I heard, he was dating
the most beautiful girl on campus.

596
00:36:30,323 --> 00:36:32,758
What happened to them?

597
00:36:36,530 --> 00:36:40,198
Oh my Gosh.

598
00:36:40,198 --> 00:36:41,767
Looks like it's just the first day of school

599
00:36:41,767 --> 00:36:44,103
and something major is happening.

600
00:36:44,103 --> 00:36:45,975
Major event?

601
00:36:45,975 --> 00:36:48,399
Well, I heard a rumor

602
00:36:48,400 --> 00:36:52,967
that there's this secret sorority
of popular girls on campus.

603
00:36:52,968 --> 00:36:56,849
They are known by the name Aylip.

604
00:36:56,849 --> 00:36:58,566
Aylip?

605
00:36:58,567 --> 00:37:01,780
Yes, they're a very powerful group.

606
00:37:01,780 --> 00:37:05,190
As in, only the cream of the crop is invited.

607
00:37:05,190 --> 00:37:07,892
These are children of the wealthiest family,

608
00:37:07,892 --> 00:37:10,895
student leaders, and top academic listers.

609
00:37:10,895 --> 00:37:17,101
And, if the rumors are correct,
if you offend any one of them,

610
00:37:17,101 --> 00:37:19,671
it's like you offended all of them.

611
00:37:19,671 --> 00:37:22,369
And, based on my sources...

612
00:37:22,369 --> 00:37:24,342
there's someone new that they're declaring

613
00:37:24,342 --> 00:37:29,347
persona-non-grata on the first day of school.

614
00:37:29,347 --> 00:37:30,963
Who?

615
00:37:34,767 --> 00:37:35,767
[TWPS]

616
00:37:43,605 --> 00:37:44,698
Oh?

617
00:37:44,698 --> 00:37:49,633
Hey! Owen, wait. We're not yet done talking.

618
00:37:57,517 --> 00:37:59,114
Alyanna...

619
00:38:00,507 --> 00:38:03,943
I saw a girl who looks exactly like you
the other day.

620
00:38:06,716 --> 00:38:10,821
I don't believe in what they say
"leap of blood" but...

621
00:38:11,693 --> 00:38:13,828
I felt something.

622
00:38:15,864 --> 00:38:18,099
Is she my grandchild?

623
00:38:19,364 --> 00:38:21,799
Is Celestina alive?

624
00:38:23,501 --> 00:38:28,639
Because if she is,
I will not stop until I find her.

625
00:39:15,275 --> 00:39:17,243
Are they looking at me?

626
00:39:18,166 --> 00:39:20,300
Is there dirt on my face?

627
00:39:21,323 --> 00:39:23,650
Well, right...

628
00:39:23,650 --> 00:39:25,029
Marian Rivera...

629
00:39:25,029 --> 00:39:27,898
Left, Bea Alonzo.

630
00:39:28,800 --> 00:39:31,197
Go ahead and get tired of at looking me.

631
00:39:31,197 --> 00:39:32,603
I'm sure you find me beautiful.

632
00:39:32,603 --> 00:39:34,238
Goodbye.

633
00:39:37,650 --> 00:39:39,585
Move aside.

634
00:39:53,519 --> 00:39:54,879
What's with my face?

635
00:39:54,879 --> 00:39:56,621
Is there really dirt?

636
00:40:00,067 --> 00:40:01,369
I'll just use the CR.

637
00:40:01,369 --> 00:40:04,105
This is off-limits.

638
00:40:04,105 --> 00:40:05,506
Off-limits?

639
00:40:05,506 --> 00:40:06,807
Why?

640
00:40:06,807 --> 00:40:10,845
I said... this is off-limits.

641
00:40:10,845 --> 00:40:12,401
Shoo.

642
00:40:13,441 --> 00:40:15,274
Shoo.

643
00:40:15,274 --> 00:40:17,620
Okay, I'll use a different comfort room.

644
00:40:17,620 --> 00:40:19,419
Girl...

645
00:40:32,833 --> 00:40:34,268
Did you do that on purpose?

646
00:40:34,268 --> 00:40:38,105
If you don't want to be hit,
find a different place,

647
00:40:38,105 --> 00:40:41,041
not here where we are playing.

648
00:41:08,736 --> 00:41:10,548
Hey!

649
00:41:10,548 --> 00:41:11,939
Who are you?

650
00:41:11,939 --> 00:41:13,376
Let go of me.

651
00:41:13,376 --> 00:41:15,243
Have you seen Florence?

652
00:41:15,243 --> 00:41:17,044
Florence is missing?

653
00:41:17,044 --> 00:41:18,713
Did you receive my messages?

654
00:41:18,713 --> 00:41:20,381
What message?

655
00:41:20,381 --> 00:41:22,472
I haven't received anything from you.

656
00:41:22,472 --> 00:41:23,894
You suddenly disappeared.

657
00:41:23,894 --> 00:41:25,885
You're right.

658
00:41:25,885 --> 00:41:27,653
This would be better for both of us.

659
00:41:27,653 --> 00:41:28,787
How's Florence?

660
00:41:28,787 --> 00:41:32,134
Well, she sent me a message.

661
00:41:32,135 --> 00:41:35,638
She said she was just fixing something.

662
00:41:36,822 --> 00:41:39,557
I'll just go here. There's a way here.

663
00:41:48,673 --> 00:41:50,164
Why are you following me?

664
00:41:50,165 --> 00:41:51,180
Show yourself.

665
00:41:51,180 --> 00:41:52,611
Do you think I'm scared of you?

666
00:41:52,611 --> 00:41:54,512
Who are you?
